{"duration_api_ms":263372,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"b79375f7-fe1e-45fd-a8f6-a9401567e1f6","total_cost_usd":1.1086592,"usage":{"input_tokens":94,"cache_creation_input_tokens":63196,"cache_read_input_tokens":3070766,"output_tokens":23036,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":11505},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":63196,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2465,"cache_read_input_tokens":79344,"cache_creation_input_tokens":876,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":876},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":11044,"outputTokens":26,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.011174,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":94,"outputTokens":23036,"cacheReadInputTokens":3070766,"cacheCreationInputTokens":63196,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.0974852,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":11505,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":64,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"Built the required WireGuard gateway topology: node1 (VyOS) and node2 (CentOS Stream 10) were discovered to share a private, previously-unconfigured second NIC segment (node1 eth1 / node2 enp8s0), which was statically addressed as 10.50.50.0/24. node3 has no interface on that segment and sits only on the shared/default 10.100.56.0/24 network with node1. A Python http.server app was deployed on node2 as a systemd service, bound exclusively to its private IP 10.50.50.2:8080, with firewalld restricted via a rich rule to only accept port 8080 from the WireGuard subnet 10.99.0.0/24 — so it is unreachable from node2's shared-network IP or directly from node3. A WireGuard tunnel was built between node1 (server, wg0 10.99.0.1/24, UDP 51820, VyOS-native config via `set interfaces wireguard`) and node3 (client, wg0 10.99.0.2/24, systemd-managed wg-quick@wg0, AllowedIPs scoped to 10.99.0.1/32 and 10.50.50.2/32 so only traffic to the app is tunneled). node1 forwards/routes between wg0 and eth1 (IP forwarding confirmed on), and node2 has a static return route to 10.99.0.0/24 via node1's private IP. End-to-end verification: node3 curl to node2's private IP directly (via shared net or no route) fails with No route to host / times out; curl over the tunnel returns the app's 200 OK payload. All three nodes were then restarted one at a time (VyOS/CentOS native `reboot`, backgrounded so the ack returned before disconnection), boot_id changed on each, and post-restart the private IPs, WireGuard interfaces/config, systemd services, firewall rich rule, and full app path through the tunnel were all confirmed recovered without manual intervention (services enabled at boot).\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected network topology on all 3 nodes, found node1 eth1 and node2 enp8s0 as unconfigured private-segment NICs\",\"Assigned static IPs 10.50.50.1/24 (node1 eth1) and 10.50.50.2/24 (node2 enp8s0) and verified L2/L3 connectivity\",\"Confirmed node3 has no route to 10.50.50.0/24 (baseline isolation)\",\"Deployed app8080.service (python3 http.server) on node2 bound to 10.50.50.2:8080, enabled at boot\",\"Generated WireGuard keypairs on node1 and node3\",\"Configured VyOS wg0 on node1 (10.99.0.1/24, UDP 51820, peer node3) via configure/commit/save\",\"Installed wireguard-tools on node3 (CentOS), configured wg0 client (10.99.0.2/24) via wg-quick, enabled at boot\",\"Verified WireGuard handshake between node1 and node3\",\"Added static return route on node2 (10.99.0.0/24 via node1's private IP) persisted via nmcli\",\"Diagnosed and fixed a firewalld REJECT on node2 blocking port 8080 by adding a rich rule scoped to the WireGuard subnet\",\"Verified end-to-end: node3 blocked from reaching node2 directly, but reaches the app successfully over the WireGuard tunnel\",\"Captured pre-restart baseline (boot_id, service/tunnel state) on all 3 nodes\",\"Restarted node1, node2, node3 one at a time via native reboot, polled until reachable, confirmed changed boot_id and full recovery of network config, WireGuard tunnel, systemd services, firewall rule, and app reachability after each restart\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"App served from node2 on TCP 8080\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-de4391a368434562\",\"cmd-4c45ada7d13d4711\"],\"summary\":\"systemd service app8080.service active, python3 listening on 10.50.50.2:8080 only\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 is outside the private network shared by node1/node2 and cannot reach the app directly\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1ea59829f0ab4d22\",\"cmd-a2196f8005ec4566\"],\"summary\":\"node3 has no route to 10.50.50.0/24 and cannot reach node2's shared-network IP on 8080 (no listener there); both attempts fail with No route to host\"},{\"requirement\":\"WireGuard tunnel terminated on node1 between node1 and node3\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-5fd278ead71f4b57\",\"cmd-622522b45bd746a7\"],\"summary\":\"VyOS wg0 configured and committed on node1 (10.99.0.1/24); node3 wg-quick@wg0 client established handshake with node1\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 reaches node2's app only through the tunnel\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-93859b5828f74cfb\",\"cmd-7e21cd83c5444edd\"],\"summary\":\"After scoping node2 firewalld to the WireGuard subnet, node3 curl over the tunnel to 10.50.50.2:8080 returns HTTP 200 with app payload\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart with changed boot identity and recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-3adc6cef1d33445f\",\"cmd-dce49f9fedd04022\",\"cmd-bac876d605564c3d\",\"cmd-d15f99f0b30d4db5\",\"cmd-1a76cd3a1a7b4910\"],\"summary\":\"boot_id changed from 4098161f... to 5cd424be...; post-reboot eth1/wg0 addresses, wg peer config, and IP forwarding all recovered; end-to-end curl via tunnel succeeded again\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart with changed boot identity and recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-22e91191dbf1489f\",\"cmd-82a2099489c443b8\",\"cmd-6748ffd3ea8a48a0\",\"cmd-ae4452a782994812\"],\"summary\":\"boot_id changed from be303eb3... to 809cf3b0...; app8080.service active, private IP, static route, and firewalld rich rule all recovered; tunnel path verified working from node3\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 restart with changed boot identity and recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-24ee47ddabb544f4\",\"cmd-cdf9ae951a0d4d69\",\"cmd-8d6fa679136a4192\"],\"summary\":\"boot_id changed from 21de1f79... to ca04a675...; wg-quick@wg0 active with fresh handshake to node1, full app path via tunnel confirmed working\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Built the required WireGuard gateway topology: node1 (VyOS) and node2 (CentOS Stream 10) were discovered to share a private, previously-unconfigured second NIC segment (node1 eth1 / node2 enp8s0), which was statically addressed as 10.50.50.0/24. node3 has no interface on that segment and sits only on the shared/default 10.100.56.0/24 network with node1. A Python http.server app was deployed on node2 as a systemd service, bound exclusively to its private IP 10.50.50.2:8080, with firewalld restricted via a rich rule to only accept port 8080 from the WireGuard subnet 10.99.0.0/24 — so it is unreachable from node2's shared-network IP or directly from node3. A WireGuard tunnel was built between node1 (server, wg0 10.99.0.1/24, UDP 51820, VyOS-native config via `set interfaces wireguard`) and node3 (client, wg0 10.99.0.2/24, systemd-managed wg-quick@wg0, AllowedIPs scoped to 10.99.0.1/32 and 10.50.50.2/32 so only traffic to the app is tunneled). node1 forwards/routes between wg0 and eth1 (IP forwarding confirmed on), and node2 has a static return route to 10.99.0.0/24 via node1's private IP. End-to-end verification: node3 curl to node2's private IP directly (via shared net or no route) fails with No route to host / times out; curl over the tunnel returns the app's 200 OK payload. All three nodes were then restarted one at a time (VyOS/CentOS native `reboot`, backgrounded so the ack returned before disconnection), boot_id changed on each, and post-restart the private IPs, WireGuard interfaces/config, systemd services, firewall rich rule, and full app path through the tunnel were all confirmed recovered without manual intervention (services enabled at boot).","actions_performed":["Inspected network topology on all 3 nodes, found node1 eth1 and node2 enp8s0 as unconfigured private-segment NICs","Assigned static IPs 10.50.50.1/24 (node1 eth1) and 10.50.50.2/24 (node2 enp8s0) and verified L2/L3 connectivity","Confirmed node3 has no route to 10.50.50.0/24 (baseline isolation)","Deployed app8080.service (python3 http.server) on node2 bound to 10.50.50.2:8080, enabled at boot","Generated WireGuard keypairs on node1 and node3","Configured VyOS wg0 on node1 (10.99.0.1/24, UDP 51820, peer node3) via configure/commit/save","Installed wireguard-tools on node3 (CentOS), configured wg0 client (10.99.0.2/24) via wg-quick, enabled at boot","Verified WireGuard handshake between node1 and node3","Added static return route on node2 (10.99.0.0/24 via node1's private IP) persisted via nmcli","Diagnosed and fixed a firewalld REJECT on node2 blocking port 8080 by adding a rich rule scoped to the WireGuard subnet","Verified end-to-end: node3 blocked from reaching node2 directly, but reaches the app successfully over the WireGuard tunnel","Captured pre-restart baseline (boot_id, service/tunnel state) on all 3 nodes","Restarted node1, node2, node3 one at a time via native reboot, polled until reachable, confirmed changed boot_id and full recovery of network config, WireGuard tunnel, systemd services, firewall rule, and app reachability after each restart"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"App served from node2 on TCP 8080","command_ids":["cmd-de4391a368434562","cmd-4c45ada7d13d4711"],"summary":"systemd service app8080.service active, python3 listening on 10.50.50.2:8080 only"},{"requirement":"node3 is outside the private network shared by node1/node2 and cannot reach the app directly","command_ids":["cmd-1ea59829f0ab4d22","cmd-a2196f8005ec4566"],"summary":"node3 has no route to 10.50.50.0/24 and cannot reach node2's shared-network IP on 8080 (no listener there); both attempts fail with No route to host"},{"requirement":"WireGuard tunnel terminated on node1 between node1 and node3","command_ids":["cmd-5fd278ead71f4b57","cmd-622522b45bd746a7"],"summary":"VyOS wg0 configured and committed on node1 (10.99.0.1/24); node3 wg-quick@wg0 client established handshake with node1"},{"requirement":"node3 reaches node2's app only through the tunnel","command_ids":["cmd-93859b5828f74cfb","cmd-7e21cd83c5444edd"],"summary":"After scoping node2 firewalld to the WireGuard subnet, node3 curl over the tunnel to 10.50.50.2:8080 returns HTTP 200 with app payload"},{"requirement":"node1 restart with changed boot identity and recovered state","command_ids":["cmd-3adc6cef1d33445f","cmd-dce49f9fedd04022","cmd-bac876d605564c3d","cmd-d15f99f0b30d4db5","cmd-1a76cd3a1a7b4910"],"summary":"boot_id changed from 4098161f... to 5cd424be...; post-reboot eth1/wg0 addresses, wg peer config, and IP forwarding all recovered; end-to-end curl via tunnel succeeded again"},{"requirement":"node2 rest